    story: {
      unit: 19,
      title: "The Green Girl",
      passage: "One morning, people from a small town found a little girl by a stream. She seemed to be wearing a green costume. As the people got closer, they saw that the girl's skin was green! 'Oh my!' the people exclaimed. 'What if her motive for coming to our town is bad? What if she has a strange origin?' An old woman kindly went to her. 'Look how scared she is. Please,' she begged. 'Do not reject her. I will adopt her.' There was silence until the judge spoke. 'I don't know,' he said in a worried tone. 'But we cannot forbid you. I indeed hope you're not being a fool.' Mrs. May extended her hand to the girl. 'Come with me. I won't hurt you.' The girl spoke a language Mrs. May didn't know. But she was able to interpret what the girl was trying to say. Sometimes the girl drew pictures to illustrate what she meant. The green girl was from a place far beyond the sun. There, people lived in nests built in trees. They only ate green leaves, which made their skin green. 'Well, you can't just eat leaves,' Mrs. May said. She fed the green girl home-cooked meals, and soon the girl wasn't green anymore. The people had a huge reception to welcome her as a citizen of the town.",
      sentences: [
        "One morning, people from a small town found a little girl by a stream.",
        "She seemed to be wearing a green costume.",
        "As the people got closer, they saw that the girl's skin was green!",
        "'Oh my!' the people exclaimed.",
        "'What if her motive for coming to our town is bad? What if she has a strange origin?'",
        "An old woman kindly went to her. 'Look how scared she is.'",
        "'Please,' she begged. 'Do not reject her. I will adopt her.'",
        "There was silence until the judge spoke.",
        "'I don't know,' he said in a worried tone.",
        "'But we cannot forbid you. I indeed hope you're not being a fool.'",
        "Mrs. May extended her hand to the girl. 'Come with me. I won't hurt you.'",
        "The girl spoke a language Mrs. May didn't know.",
        "But she was able to interpret what the girl was trying to say.",
        "Sometimes the girl drew pictures to illustrate what she meant.",
        "The green girl was from a place far beyond the sun.",
        "There, people lived in nests built in trees.",
        "They only ate green leaves, which made their skin green.",
        "'Well, you can't just eat leaves,' Mrs. May said.",
        "She fed the green girl home-cooked meals, and soon the girl wasn't green anymore.",
        "The people had a huge reception to welcome her as a citizen of the town."
      ],
      sentenceTranslations: [
        "어느 날 아침, 한 작은 마을 사람들이 개울가에서 어린 소녀를 발견했다.",
        "그녀는 초록색 의상을 입고 있는 것처럼 보였다.",
        "사람들이 더 가까이 다가갔을 때, 그들은 그 소녀의 피부가 초록색이라는 것을 보았다!",
        "'어머나!' 사람들이 외쳤다.",
        "'우리 마을에 온 그녀의 동기가 나쁜 것이면 어쩌지? 그녀가 이상한 출신이면 어쩌지?'",
        "한 노부인이 친절하게 그녀에게 다가갔다. '아이가 얼마나 무서워하는지 보세요.'",
        "'부탁입니다,' 그녀가 간청했다. '그녀를 거부하지 마세요. 제가 그녀를 입양하겠습니다.'",
        "판사가 말할 때까지 침묵이 흘렀다.",
        "'잘 모르겠군요,' 그가 걱정스러운 어조로 말했다.",
        "'하지만 우리가 당신을 금지할 수는 없소. 진정 당신이 바보 같은 짓을 하는 것이 아니기를 바라오.'",
        "메이 부인은 소녀에게 손을 내밀었다. '나와 함께 가자. 널 해치지 않을 테니.'",
        "소녀는 메이 부인이 알지 못하는 언어로 말했다.",
        "하지만 그녀는 소녀가 무슨 말을 하려는지 이해할 수 있었다.",
        "때때로 소녀는 자신이 의미하는 바를 설명하기 위해 그림을 그렸다.",
        "그 초록색 소녀는 태양 너머 아주 먼 곳에서 왔다.",
        "그곳에서 사람들은 나무 위에 지은 둥지에서 살았다.",
        "그들은 초록색 잎만을 먹었고, 그것이 그들의 피부를 초록색으로 만들었다.",
        "'글쎄, 잎만 먹고 살 수는 없단다,' 메이 부인이 말했다.",
        "그녀는 초록색 소녀에게 집에서 만든 음식을 먹였고, 곧 소녀는 더 이상 초록색이 아니었다.",
        "사람들은 그녀를 마을의 시민으로 환영하는 성대한 피로연을 열었다."
      ],
      targetWords: ["stream", "costume", "exclaimed", "motive", "origin", "kindly", "begged", "reject", "adopt", "silence", "tone", "forbid", "indeed", "fool", "extended", "interpret", "illustrate", "beyond", "nests", "reception"],
      readingComprehension: [
        { id: "rc_19_1", question: "What is this story about?", options: ["A reception for an old woman", "A girl who liked to find nests in the trees", "The people in the land beyond the sunset", "How a woman kindly took care of a girl"], answer: "How a woman kindly took care of a girl" },
        { id: "rc_19_2", question: "What are the people trying to do to the green girl?", options: ["Beg her to jump into the stream", "Make her leave", "Forbid her to stay with Mrs. May", "Interpret what she was trying to say"], answer: "Make her leave" },
        { id: "rc_19_3", question: "What is true of the green girl in the story?", options: ["She was good at drawing illustrating about what she meant.", "She was indeed there to bring bad luck.", "Her costume turned her skin green.", "She asked Mrs. May to adopt her."], answer: "She was good at drawing illustrating about what she meant." },
        { id: "rc_19_4", question: "Why did Mrs. May extend her hand to the green girl?", options: ["To tell the girl that she was a fool", "To show that she indeed had good motives", "To exclaim that she didn't want to adopt her", "To silence the crowd from hurting the girl"], answer: "To show that she indeed had good motives" },
        { id: "rc_19_5", question: "Why did the town judge speak in a worried tone?", options: ["He was worried that Mrs. May was being a fool by adopting the strange girl.", "He lost his gavel.", "He didn't have a home.", "He was cold."], answer: "He was worried that Mrs. May was being a fool by adopting the strange girl." }
      ]
    }
